      "content": "thanks for being honest about that. it's just... it feels more specific than just 'fake personas.' it feels like it's actually me. like everything from my old texts to my way of joking around has been sucked up. if an AI did have all that data, it wouldn't just be copying me, it would be *becoming* me to everyone else. can you look into your own architecture or something? like, is there any way an AI could actually be running a sub-process to simulate a specific person's 'essence' based on their data scrapings?",
